ckgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 97590, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 51251, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Romeo Santos", "streams": 31781, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Black Eyed Peas", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "reggaeton": {"genre": "reggaeton", "country_code": "sv", "country_name": "El Salvador", "summary": "Reggaeton (reggaet\u00f3n, reguet\u00f3n) is a form of urban music that became popular with Latin American youth in the early 1990s. After its mainstream exposure in 2004, it spread to North American, European and Asian audiences. Reggaeton's predecessor originated in Panama as reggae en espa\u00f1ol. After the music's gradual exposure in Puerto Rico, it eventually evolved into a new musical style known as reggaeton [1]. Reggaeton blends West-Indian music influences of reggae and dancehall with those of Latin America.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 97590, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 83414, "best_position": 6}, {"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 51251, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": 30915, "best_position": 57}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": 23946, "best_position": 51}, {"artist": "Peso Pluma", "streams": 19826, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "Tainy", "streams": 17305, "best_position": 40}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 17197, "best_position": 52}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 13141, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Feid", "streams": 10109, "best_position": 30}, {"artist": "Don Omar", "streams": 8167, "best_position": 62}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "rock": {"genre": "rock", "country_code": "sv", "country_name": "El Salvador", "summary": "Rock music is a form of popular music with a prominent vocal melody, accompanied by guitar, drums, and bass. Many styles of rock music also use keyboard instruments such as organ, piano, mellotron, and synthesizers. Other instruments sometimes utilized in rock include saxophone, harmonica, violin, flute, French horn, banjo, melodica, and timpani. Also, less common stringed instruments such as mandolin and sitar are used. Rock music usually has a strong back beat.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 17197, "best_position": 52}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "soul": {"genre": "soul", "country_code": "sv", "country_name": "El Salvador", "summary": "Soul music is a music genre that combines rhythm and blues and gospel music, originating in the United States.  According to the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, soul is \"music that arose out of the black experience in America through the transmutation of gospel and rhythm & blues into a form of funky, secular testifying.\" The genre occasionally uses improvisational additions, twirls and auxiliary sounds. Catchy rhythms, stressed by handclaps and plastic body moves, are an important feature.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kali Uchis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Mar\u00edas", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "synth-pop": {"genre": "synth-pop", "country_code": "sv", "country_name": "El Salvador", "summary": "Synth Pop was one of the most distinctive subgenres of new wave. In the early '80s, a number of bands primarily British and heavily influenced Roxy Music and David Bowie adapted the electronic innovations of bands like Kraftwerk for pop songs. Initially, in the hands of artists like Gary Numan, The Human League and Depeche Mode, the sound was eerie, sterile, and vaguely menacing, since the electronics droned on relentlessly without any change in inflections.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "be